    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded by thirteen British colonies in 1776, it was the first modern republic built on a written national constitution.</li><li>It expanded across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> by purchase, war and the dispossession of Native nations; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> ended only after civil war.</li><li>Victory in the two world wars made it a superpower, and after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1991 it was the only one.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">Constitution of the United States</a>, in force since 1789, is the oldest written national constitution still in use.</p></aside>
    </section>

